              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, the Court asked whether disparate impact alone can give rise to a permissible inference of intentional discrimination in age\u2011discrimination cases."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justices questioned whether an intent requirement is necessary for age\u2011discrimination claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souder",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souder, justice Souder questioned whether the inclusion of the word \u201creasonable\u201d implies an \u201cunreasonable\u201d defense and what that means for liability."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether an employer with an unreasonable criterion that harms older workers would face a sanction."
      }
