            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that disparate impact should be an available method of proof in age\u2011discrimination cases under the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners allege that the employer\u2019s reduction\u2011in\u2011force had a disparate impact on older workers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioners contend that mixed\u2011motive analysis raises a question about whether an employer\u2019s illegal motive caused an illegal action."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents argue that the statutory language requires an intent requirement and cannot be read in isolation from the rest of the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondents, respondents assert that the phrase \u201creasonable factors other than age\u201d signals an intent requirement, distinguishing disparate\u2011treatment from impact cases."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondents maintain that the reasonableness of a nondiscriminatory factor is a permissible consideration for a judge or jury."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3ad9b9391c00f25f506f6cec8587e25629a04ce0f438f9118347f23dc1529d39",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3ad9b9391c00-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondents argue that the case turns on whether the statute embraces a disparate\u2011impact test."
      }
    ],
